        "problem": "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & 1.5 & 2 \\\\ -3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & 1.5 & 2 \\\\ -3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
